r methodology of the data collection.\n\nI'll need to dig deeper into the footnotes and context to understand why these numbers differ so substantially. The variations could be due to different reporting methods, data revisions, or potential errors in compilation.\n\nThe key figures for fiscal years 1939-1941 show some interesting patterns:\n- 1939: 38.05% duty rate\n- 1940: 36.96% duty rate\n- 1941: 38.11% duty rate\n\nI'll continue investigating to ensure I'm using the most reliable and consistent data source for my analysis.\n\nThe discrepancy between the two bulletins for 1940 values is significant - one shows 919,709 and the other 319,709. I need to carefully verify which source provides the most accurate information.\n\nMy calculations for the centered moving average will require precise data selection, so I'll double-check each source to ensure accuracy.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_1ebc5dbd4976433697ba7018","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"ls /app/resources/*.txt | head -20"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
