gures. I'll need to investigate why there's such a large difference in the import values between these two documents.\n\nThe data reveals multiple conflicting numbers for the same fiscal years, with variations ranging from hundreds of thousands to nearly a million. This suggests I should meticulously compare the source documents to ensure accuracy and understand the source of these differences.\n\nI'll focus on calculating the duty rate using the available data points from the 1940 bulletin, specifically cross-referencing the total duties and taxes with the total value of dutiable and taxable imports for each fiscal year.\n\nThe key calculation will involve dividing the total duties by the total import values to determine the precise duty rate, ensuring I'm using consistent and verified figures from a single source document.\n\nFor FY1939 and FY1940, I'll compute the rates by performing the division and converting to a percentage, which will help me establish a clear pattern of duty rate changes between these two fiscal years.\n\nI want to verify the FY1941 data by examining the relevant Treasury Bulletin page, specifically looking at the 1941 document's page 64 to confirm the total duties, taxes, and import values for that fiscal year.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_a679946f8e794f33b0735d63","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\n# Based on the data from Treasury Bulletins\n\n# From 1940 bulletin page 21 - Fiscal Year data\n# FY1939\nfy1939_duties_taxes = 312095  # thousands of dollars\nfy1939_import_value = 820157  # thousands of dollars\n\n# FY1940\nfy1940_duties_taxes = 340006  # thousands of dollars\nfy1940_import_value = 919709  # thousands of dollars\n\n# From 1941 bulletin page 64 - Fiscal Year data\n# FY1941\nfy1941_duties_taxes = 385306  # thousands of dollars\nfy1941_import_value = 1011262  # thousands of dollars (from table 2)\n\n# Calculate duty rates\nrate_1939 = fy1939_duties_taxes / fy1939_import_value\nrate_1940 = fy1940_duties_taxes / fy1940_import_value\nrate_1941 = fy1941_duties_taxes / fy1941_import_value\n\nprint(f\"FY1939 duty rate: {rate_1939:.6f}\")\nprint(f\"FY1940 duty rate: {rate_1940:.6f}\")\nprint(f\"FY1941 duty rate: {rate_1941:.6f}\")\n\n# For 3-year centered moving average centered on 1940:\n# (rate_1939 + rate_1940 + rate_1941) / 3\ncma = (rate_1939 + rate_1940 + rate_1941) / 3\nprint(f\"\\nCentered Moving Average (centered on 1940): {cma:.6f}\")\nprint(f\"Rounded to 3 decimal places: {cma:.3f}\")\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
