duties only) / (Total value of dutiable imports only, excluding taxable)\n\n\n- Or: (Total duties and taxes) / (Total value of dutiable and taxable imports)\n\nI'll use the most straightforward approach: (Total duties and taxes) / (Total value of dutiable and taxable imports). This gives us an effective rate across all goods with customs obligations.\n\nI'll verify the 1941 figures, noting the slight discrepancy between bulletins in the total value of dutiable imports.\n\nThe 1940 bulletin shows a total value of 919,709, while the 1941 bulletin presents a different number. I'll proceed with 1,011,262 from the 1941 bulletin for the most recent data.\n\nI'm investigating whether the rates might involve free list items, but the available data seems limited. I'll calculate the rates using the existing figures and complete the centered moving average calculation.\n\nThe current calculation shows a centered moving average of 0.377, which seems too low for historical tariff rates. I'll scrutinize the data more carefully to ensure accuracy, particularly focusing on the value of dutiable imports.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_b5d87a12ad0b47c9bba0b890","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\n# Let me verify the data again more carefully\n\n# From page 21 of 1940 bulletin:\n# Table shows:\n# - Total duties and taxes for FY1939: 312,095 (thousands)\n# - Total value of dutiable and taxable imports for FY1939: 820,157 (thousands)\n# - Total duties and taxes for FY1940: 340,006 (thousands) \n# - Total value of dutiable and taxable imports for FY1940: 919,709 (thousands)\n\n# From page 64 of 1941 bulletin:\n# Table shows:\n# - Total duties and taxes for FY1940: 340,006 (thousands)\n# - Total duties and taxes for FY1941: 385,306 (thousands)\n# - Total value of dutiable and taxable imports for FY1940: 319,709 (thousands) -- this seems wrong compared to 1940 bulletin\n# - Total value of dutiable and taxable imports for FY1941: 1,011,262 (thousands)\n\n# Note: The FY1940 value differs between bulletins - using consistent source\n# Using values from 1940 bulletin for FY1940 consistency\n\n# Values from 1940 bulletin (page 21):\nfy1939_duties = 312095\nfy1939_imports = 820157\n\nfy1940_duties = 340006\nfy1940_imports = 919709\n\n# Values from 1941 bulletin (page 64):\nfy1941_duties = 385306\nfy1941_imports = 1011262\n\n# Calculate rates\nrate_1939 = fy1939_duties / fy1939_imports\nrate_1940 = fy1940_duties / fy1940_imports\nrate_1941 = fy1941_duties / fy1941_imports\n\nprint(f\"FY1939: Duties={fy1939_duties}, Imports={fy1939_imports}, Rate={rate_1939:.6f}\")\nprint(f\"FY1940: Duties={fy1940_duties}, Imports={fy1940_imports}, Rate={rate_1940:.6f}\")\nprint(f\"FY1941: Duties={fy1941_duties}, Imports={fy1941_imports}, Rate={rate_1941:.6f}\")\n\n# Centered moving average with window of 3 (centered on 1940)\n# CMA(t) = (y(t-1) + y(t) + y(t+1)) / 3\n# CMA for 1940 = (1939 + 1940 + 1941) / 3\n\ncma = (rate_1939 + rate_1940 + rate_1941) / 3\nprint(f\"\\nCentered Moving Average (FY1939-1941, centered on 1940):\")\nprint(f\"CMA = ({rate_1939:.6f} + {rate_1940:.6f} + {rate_1941:.6f}) / 3\")\nprint(f\"CMA = {cma:.6f}\")\nprint(f\"Rounded to 3 decimal places: {cma:.3f}\")\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
